0","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1006\/jcat.1993.1322"},{"key":"2024012010051386100_r11","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/0021-9517(89)90034-1"},{"key":"2024012010051386100_r12","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/S0167-2738(96)00574-7"},{"key":"2024012010051386100_r13","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1023\/A:1019020614336"},{"key":"2024012010051386100_r14"},{"key":"2024012010051386100_r15"}],"container-title":["Chemistry Letters"],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/academic.oup.com\/chemlett\/article-pdf\/32\/9\/822\/55580898\/cl.2003.822.pdf","content-type":"application\/pdf","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"syndication"},{"URL":"https:\/\/academic.oup.com\/chemlett\/article-pdf\/32\/9\/822\/55580898\/cl.2003.822.pdf","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2024,1,20]],"date-time":"2024-01-20T10:06:45Z","timestamp":1705745205000},"score":43.273746,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/academic.oup.com\/chemlett\/article\/32\/9\/822\/7383348"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2003,8,11]]},"references-count":15,"journal-issue":{"issue":"9","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2003,8,11]]},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2003,9,1]]}},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1246\/cl.2003.822","ISSN":["0366-7022","1348-0715"],"issn-type":[{"value":"0366-7022","type":"print"},{"value":"1348-0715","type":"electronic"}],"published-other":{"date-parts":[[2003,9]]},"published":{"date-parts":[[2003,8,11]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2023,4,16]],"date-time":"2023-04-16T18:53:28Z","timestamp":1681671208149},"reference-count":12,"publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media LLC","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2011,2,1]],"date-time":"2011-02-01T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1296518400000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":3318,"URL":"https:\/\/www.cambridge.org\/core\/terms"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["MRS Proc."],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2002]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title><jats:p>The catalytic properties of nanostructured gold catalyst are known to depend on the size of the gold particles and to be activated when the size decreases to a few nanometers. We investigated the size dependence of the three-dimensional nanostructure on the mean inner potential of gold catalysts supported on titanium oxide using electron holography and high-resolution electron microscopy (HREM). The contact angle of the gold particles on the titanium oxide tended to be over 90\u00b0 for gold particles with a size of over 5 nm, and below 90\u00b0 for a size of below 2 nm. This decreasing change in the contact angle (morphology) acts to increase the perimeter and hence the area of the interface between the gold and titanium oxide support, which is considered to be an active site for CO oxidation. The mean inner potential of the gold particles also changed as their size decreased. The value of the inner potential of gold, which is approximately 25 V in bulk state, rose to over 40 V when the size of the gold particles was less than 2 nm. This phenomenon indicates the existence of a charge transfer at the interface between gold and titanium oxide. The 3-D structure change and the inner potential change should be attributed to the specific electronic structure at the interface, owing to both the \u201cnano size effect\u201d and the \u201chetero-interface effect.\u201d<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1557\/proc-727-r2.2","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2019,6,6]],"date-time":"2019-06-06T19:35:42Z","timestamp":1559849742000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":3,"title":["Electron Holographic Nano-Characterization of Gold Catalyst at Interface"],"prefix":"10.1557","volume":"727","author":[{"given":"S.","family":"Ichikawa","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"T.","family":"Akita","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"M.","family":"Okumura","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"M.","family":"Haruta","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"K.","family":"Tanaka","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"297","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2011,2,1]]},"reference":[{"key":"S1946427400130052_ref002","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/sia.959"},{"key":"S1946427400130052_ref012","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.2320\/jinstmet1952.60.7_693"},{"key":"S1946427400130052_ref010","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1107\/S0567739470000050"},{"key":"S1946427400130052_ref008","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1093\/oxfordjournals.jmicro.a023855"},{"key":"S1946427400130052_ref001","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/S0920-5861(96)00208-8"},{"key":"S1946427400130052_ref003","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/S0167-2991(06)81759-3"},{"key":"S1946427400130052_ref005","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/BF01378072"},{"key":"S1946427400130052_ref006","volume-title":"presented at Microscopy Society of America meeting 1997","author":"Wang","year":"1997"},{"key":"S1946427400130052_ref007","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/978-1-4615-4817-1_12"},{"key":"S1946427400130052_ref009","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1107\/S0108767392005087"},{"key":"S1946427400130052_ref011","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1006\/jcat.1993.1322"},{"key":"S1946427400130052_ref004","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/BF01333120"}],"container-title":["MRS Proceedings"],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/www.cambridge.org\/core\/services\/aop-cambridge-core\/content\/view\/S1946427400130052","content-type":"unspecifie